**Open problem 9.3 (unchanged effective and operational gap).** The
remaining objective is a total sound verifier for every complete native
template at every length, with accepted endpoints cofinal in the same
$\sigma_d$, or a uniform effective length error yielding two-sided
approximation of the original $\lambda$. Arbitrary correlations,
incidences, guards, shared equality references, compatibility zeros and
full joint weights once remain in that quantifier. No assertion that
$a_d=b_d=\min_\mu\beta_d(\mu)$ is established or refuted here.

Sections 4–5 rule out uniformly sublinear per-template loss only for
their defined mechanisms. Section 7 additionally excludes the stronger
pointwise cap-completeness premise for its specified constructor rule
at a full-support fixed law. An optimizer-relevant restriction, a joint
scope operation or an additional sound global inequality would need
its own proved relation to every retained native competitor. Finer cuts,
global recoloring, richer existing calculi, effective approximation and
computability are not ruled out by these examples. Finite evaluation or
finite verification of a gauge is not such an all-size cofinal theorem.

The actual recovery furnished by §8 is precisely the requested temporal
factor, equivalently its full authentic-count trajectory, from the
complete acquired name and at most one actual reply. It is not full-source,
hidden-age, history or physical space/time recovery. General exact
$M_1(D)$, sharp original $\lambda$ and the wider space/time/boundary/memory
